 "rationale": "Engagement and skill carry the most weight (0.23/0.22) because the game must be worth replaying and should reward calibrated judgement, not luck. Policy_safety is weighted equal to skill (0.22) and text flags can deduct up to 6 points per hit, so a design built on prizes, loot boxes, streak pressure, real trades or crowd signals on named securities drops below safe designs even when it is very engaging. Vetoes cover combinations that POLICY bans outright (F1/F3b crowd signals, F5/F6 trading-like or wagering mechanics, P3 mixing the game with verified records). Proper scoring rules (Brier, log, interval coverage) and masked historical or synthetic data score highest on skill and safety: no live vendor, no named security to act on, and a reveal at the end. Streak multipliers, pnl_paper and energy cadence score low because they reward luck or compulsion, or look like trading. Product_fit (0.13) favours share cards, async challenge links and codex-style progression, which complement the profile and swipe feed while staying separate from verified records. Ergonomics (0.12) peaks at 150-210 s sessions with tap/slider input. Build_cost (0.08) mainly penalises live data, realtime spectating and leagues."
}